-- Sale of Food Act 1973 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
-- Expected values worked by hand from ../source/SFA1973.txt.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN consumed IS A BOOLEAN, ex IS AN `Excluded product`, contact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Article
`article` consumed ex contact MEANS Article OF consumed, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ex, contact

`rice` MEANS `article` TRUE `none` FALSE
`a cough syrup` MEANS `article` TRUE `a medicinal product` FALSE
`a cooking pot` MEANS `article` FALSE `none` TRUE
`a toy` MEANS `article` FALSE `none` FALSE

GIVEN handles IS A BOOLEAN, excluded IS A BOOLEAN, retail IS A BOOLEAN, component IS A BOOLEAN, primary IS A BOOLEAN, licensed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Business facts`
`business` handles excluded retail component primary licensed MEANS `Business facts` OF handles, excluded, retail, component, primary, licensed

`a sauce factory` MEANS `business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a hawker stall` MEANS `business` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a farm` MEANS `business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN Article, c IS A Conduct, repeat IS A BOOLEAN, steps IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A MAYBE `Warranty facts`
GIVETH A `Food case`
`case` a c repeat steps w MEANS `Food case` OF a, c, repeat, steps, w, TRUE

GIVEN reliance IS A BOOLEAN, abroad IS A BOOLEAN, believed IS A BOOLEAN, prosecutor IS A MAYBE DATE, warrantor IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Warranty facts`
`warranty` reliance abroad believed prosecutor warrantor MEANS `Warranty facts` OF reliance, TRUE, TRUE, abroad, believed, (YMD 2026 3 1), prosecutor, warrantor

§§ `Goal 1 — what the Act reaches`

#ASSERT `food` `rice`
-- s 2A(3)(b): a medicinal product is not food; s 2A(3)(g): a package is not, edible packaging aside
#ASSERT NOT `food` `a cough syrup`
#ASSERT NOT `food` (`article` TRUE `a package (not edible packaging)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `food` `a cooking pot`
-- s 2A(1)(e): declared food
#ASSERT `food` (Article OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `none`, FALSE)
-- s 2C: likely harm when used as intended; not merely an allergy
#ASSERT `unsafe` (`Safety facts` OF TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `unsafe` (`Safety facts` OF TRUE, TRUE)
-- s 2D: unexpected foreign matter; lawful chemical residue is not unsuitable
#ASSERT `unsuitable` (`Suitability facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `unsuitable` (`Suitability facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `adulterated` (`Adulteration facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `adulterated` (`Adulteration facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- s 2B, 2F: a factory supplying wholesalers is non-retail; a hawker stall is retail; a farm is primary production
#ASSERT `a non-retail food business` `a sauce factory`
#ASSERT NOT `a non-retail food business` `a hawker stall`
#ASSERT `a non-retail food business` (`business` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a non-retail food business` `a farm`
#ASSERT `a food business` `a farm`
#ASSERT NOT `a food business` (`business` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 2E(2)
#ASSERT NOT `a sale within the Act` `a personal, non-commercial exchange`
#ASSERT `a sale within the Act` `a sale or other dealing listed in s 2E(1)`

§§ `Goal 2 — offences and penalties`

-- s 14: more than 50 parts per million
#ASSERT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling food with methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol` 51)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling food with methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol` 50)
-- s 11: adulterated food sold with full disclosure is lawful
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling adulterated food` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling adulterated food` FALSE)
-- s 15: knew or ought reasonably to have known
#ASSERT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling unsafe food` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`selling unsafe food` FALSE)
-- s 21: an unlicensed non-retail business; a retail stall needs no Part 4 licence
#ASSERT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`carrying on a food business` `a sauce factory`)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`carrying on a food business` `a hawker stall`)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`carrying on a food business` (`business` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- s 33(5)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`giving a false written warranty` TRUE)

-- s 49: $5,000; repeat $10,000 or 3 months
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions` `, a second or subsequent conviction:` FALSE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions` `, a second or subsequent conviction:` TRUE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 10000, 3, 0
-- s 10K(2), (4); s 48(3); s 56(1)(r)
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` (`failing to comply with a food safety direction` FALSE) `, a second or subsequent conviction:` FALSE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 10000, 12, 0
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` (`removing a direction affixed to food premises` TRUE) `, a second or subsequent conviction:` TRUE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 6, 0
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` `refusing or mis-stating name and address` `, a second or subsequent conviction:` FALSE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 300, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for` `contravening food regulations` `, a second or subsequent conviction:` FALSE EQUALS `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 0, 500
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` TRUE EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Goal 3 — defences and liability`

-- s 33: notice to the prosecutor and the warrantor within 7 days of service (1 March): 8 March in time, 9 March late
#ASSERT `the warranty defence is made out` (`warranty` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)))
#ASSERT NOT `the warranty defence is made out` (`warranty` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 9)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)))
#ASSERT NOT `the warranty defence is made out` (`warranty` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 8)) NOTHING)
-- s 33(2): a warrantor abroad needs the accused's reasonable steps and belief
#ASSERT NOT `the warranty defence is made out` (`warranty` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)))
#ASSERT `the warranty defence is made out` (`warranty` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)))
-- s 16A(6)-(7): a broadcaster with no control has a defence, unless warned
#ASSERT `the carrier or publisher defence is made out` (`publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier or publisher defence is made out` (`publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 32: reasonable steps answer a selling charge, not a licensing charge
#ASSERT `a defence answers the charge` (`case` `rice` `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions` FALSE TRUE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `a defence answers the charge` (`case` `rice` (`carrying on a food business` `a sauce factory`) FALSE TRUE NOTHING)
-- s 33 applies only to Part 3
#ASSERT NOT `a defence answers the charge` (`case` `rice` (`failing to comply with a food safety direction` FALSE) FALSE FALSE (JUST (`warranty` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)))))
#ASSERT `the named importer, maker or packer is liable as seller, unopened package:` TRUE `, named:` TRUE `, proved otherwise:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the named importer, maker or packer is liable as seller, unopened package:` FALSE `, named:` TRUE `, proved otherwise:` FALSE

§§ `Goal 4 — procedure`

#ASSERT `a complaint about a seizure is still in time, hours since seizure` 48
#ASSERT NOT `a complaint about a seizure is still in time, hours since seizure` 49
#ASSERT `the seized article passes to the Agency, complained in time:` FALSE `, confirmed:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the seized article passes to the Agency, complained in time:` TRUE `, confirmed:` FALSE
#ASSERT `a direction may be given to` `an importer or exporter of food or a food contact article`
#ASSERT NOT `a direction may be given to` `another person`
-- s 10C(4)(c): published 10 June, in effect 11 June
#ASSERT `the direction takes effect on, manner` (`published in the news media and on the Agency's website` (YMD 2026 6 10)) `, served on` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 11
#ASSERT `the direction takes effect on, manner` `served on the person` `, served on` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `the direction is in force on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, expiring` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, revoked` NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the direction is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, expiring` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, revoked` NOTHING
-- s 10I: received 1 June; deemed refused after 29 June; review by 13 July; or 14 days after notification
#ASSERT `the application is taken as refused after, received` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 29
#ASSERT `the last day to seek review of compensation, application received` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, determination notified` NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2026 7 13
#ASSERT `the last day to seek review of compensation, application received` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, determination notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 4
#ASSERT `the court to review compensation, sought` 300000 `, District Court limit` 250000 EQUALS "the General Division of the High Court"
-- s 46(9): 4.5 months counts as 5: $1,200 x 5/12 = $500
#ASSERT `the proportionate licence fee for` 4.5 `months, annual fee` 1200 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the most financial penalty on a licensee, breach of a condition:` TRUE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the licence may be revoked or suspended under s 22(6), licensee infectious:` FALSE `, employs infectious:` TRUE `, refused:` FALSE `, not immunised:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an administrative exemption may be given, negligible risk:` TRUE `, safeguards:` TRUE `, other law:` TRUE `, trade:` FALSE
-- s 45: 7 days, stayed; s 46(14): 14 days
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal against` `another notice, order or decision of the Director-General` `, decided on` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 8)
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal against` `a licence refusal, suspension, cancellation, financial penalty or forfeiture` `, decided on` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal against` `a Part 2A direction` `, decided on` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an appeal stays the decision` `another notice, order or decision of the Director-General`
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal stays the decision` `a Part 2A direction`
#ASSERT `the appeal lies to` `a sentence or order of a District or Magistrate's Court` EQUALS "the General Division of the High Court (s 39)"
-- s 30(1): served 1 June, returnable 15 June at the earliest
#ASSERT `the summons is returnable late enough, served` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, returnable` (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the summons is returnable late enough, served` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, returnable` (YMD 2026 6 14)
-- s 34(1): returnable 15 June; 3 clear days (12, 13, 14) — notice by 11 June
#ASSERT `notice was given 3 clear days before, notice` (YMD 2026 6 11) `, returnable` (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT `notice was given 3 clear days before, notice` (YMD 2026 6 12) `, returnable` (YMD 2026 6 15)

§§ `The top-level goal`

-- a stall selling unsafe rice, knowingly, first offence: $5,000; compound up to $1,000
`unsafe rice` MEANS `the food position for` (`case` `rice` (`selling unsafe food` TRUE) FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `unsafe rice`'s `the conduct contravenes the Act`
#ASSERT NOT `unsafe rice`'s `a defence answers the charge`
#ASSERT `unsafe rice`'s `maximum penalty` EQUALS JUST (`SFA penalty` OF 5000, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `unsafe rice`'s `most that may be collected to compound` EQUALS JUST 1000
-- selling a toy is not within the selling offences
`a toy sold` MEANS `the food position for` (`case` `a toy` `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions` FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `a toy sold`'s `the Act reaches the article`
#ASSERT `a toy sold`'s `maximum penalty` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a cooking pot is a food contact article: s 40 reaches it
#ASSERT (`the food position for` (`case` `a cooking pot` (`importing, advertising or selling a prohibited food contact article` FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE NOTHING))'s `maximum penalty` EQUALS JUST (`SFA penalty` OF 10000, 3, 0)
-- obstruction reaches the person, whatever the article
#ASSERT (`the food position for` (`case` `a toy` (`obstructing an officer, or interfering with an official mark` FALSE) FALSE FALSE NOTHING))'s `the conduct contravenes the Act`
-- an insanitary sale defended under s 32: no penalty
#ASSERT (`the food position for` (`case` `rice` `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions` FALSE TRUE NOTHING))'s `maximum penalty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the courts that may try an offence and impose the full penalty` EQUALS LIST "a District Court", "a Magistrate's Court"

§§ `Conditions added after the independent pass`

-- s 10K(1): with a reasonable excuse, no offence; s 10K(3): after the direction ends, none
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`failing to comply with a food safety direction` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`removing a direction affixed to food premises` FALSE)
-- s 41(2): with authority; s 6(3), 7(1)(b): a demand the officer could not lawfully make
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`obstructing an officer, or interfering with an official mark` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`refusing to give a sample` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the conduct contravenes the Act` (`refusing to give a sample` TRUE)
